# Normain Competitor Accuracy Benchmark — Overview

Goal: produce a credible report showing Normain extracts/assesses complex documents more accurately than other AI tools. One-time benchmark, not infra.

Path: `projects/benchmark/`

## What we're measuring

How well each tool answers ~100 realistic questions over a fixed set of complex documents. Score on:
- **Extraction** — right facts?
- **Assessment** — right reasoning/judgment?
- **Citation fidelity** — does cited source actually back the claim? (Normain's wedge)
- **Completeness** — for exhaustive-search tasks, found all of them?

## Use cases (6 buckets, ~16–17 insights each)

| # | Use case | Why |
|---|---|---|
| 01 | Due-diligence financial review | Tests numerical calc, cross-doc, Excel logic |
| 02 | ESG / sustainability audit | Tests exhaustive search + numerical across long reports |
| 03 | Regulatory-vs-policy gap check | Tests cross-doc reasoning + exhaustive requirements |
| 04 | Contract clause sweep | Tests exhaustive + classification + citation fidelity |
| 05 | Board / committee composition audit | Tests cross-doc person resolution, mixed formats |
| 06 | Multimodal evidence extraction | Tests scanned, handwritten, image-only, Excel+image |

## Phases

### Phase 1 — Corpus + questions (foundation)
- Define personas/scenarios for each use case
- Source real public docs (10-Ks, ESG reports, EU AI Act, GDPR, SEC contracts, proxies, etc.)
- Synthesize gap docs (Excel logic deck, planted-clause MSA, handwritten notes, fake policy)
- Author 100 insight YAMLs (question + canonical prompt + doc refs + reasoning type)
- Lock with two-person review
- **Output**: frozen corpus + 100 locked questions

### Phase 2 — Ground truth
- Human reads each doc, writes the correct answer per question with citations
- Second human reviews each ground-truth entry against the actual doc
- **Output**: 100 ground-truth YAMLs, signed off

### Phase 3 — Competitor setup
- Decide direct-test list (Normain, Claude, ChatGPT, NotebookLM, MikeOSS, Gemini Deep Research, M365 Copilot, V7 Go — confirm)
- Decide indirect-test list (Harvey, Legora via partner)
- Provision accounts, pin plan tiers + model versions
- **Output**: `competitors/{name}.md` per tool with access details

### Phase 4 — Runs
- For each competitor: fresh account, upload corpus, run all 100 canonical prompts verbatim
- Capture per answer: prompt, text, full-session PDF, screenshot, anomaly notes
- Normain runs LAST to avoid anchoring grader expectations
- **Output**: ~1,000 raw answer artifacts under `runs/`

### Phase 5 — Grading
- Pass 1: LLM judge scores all 1,000 (cheap, fast triage)
- Pass 2: human authoritative grading on 30-insight stratified sample × all competitors (~300 events)
- Audit: human spot-checks 10% of remaining insights to calibrate judge
- Citation fidelity always human-verified on sampled set
- **Output**: per-insight per-competitor scores + disagreement log

### Phase 6 — Report
- Headline scoreboard + per-use-case + per-question-type breakdowns
- Citation fidelity deep dive (the moat)
- 5–10 paired case studies including ≥1 Normain loss for credibility
- Full methodology disclosure
- Internal version (full evidence) + public version (redacted)
- **Output**: `report/REPORT.md` + scoreboard CSV

## Current status

Phase 0 — planning. Detailed plan for Phase 1 lives at `~/.claude/plans/doc-corpus-preferably-unified-lollipop.md`.

## Key design rules

- One canonical prompt per question, identical across competitors (kills prompt bias)
- Real public docs preferred; synthesize only to plug gaps
- Corpus stays internal; report names docs but doesn't redistribute corporate reports
- Insight IDs global 001–100; flat ground-truth namespace for graders
- Plan tier + model version captured per session (drift mitigation)

